  "question": {
    "text": "The stopping potential in the context of photoelectric effect depends on the following property of incident electromagnetic radiation:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Phase",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Intensity",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Amplitude",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Frequency",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>According to Einstein&rsquo;s photoelectric equation, stopping potential depends on frequency as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mi>&#957;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mo>&#8728;</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>V</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>&#957;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mo>&#8728;</mo></msub></mrow><mi>e</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence stopping potential depends on frequency.</p>"
  }
